  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "Art Hoe fashion is embodied by a blend of vintage-inspired comfort, vibrant primary colors, and gender-neutral silhouettes. While it has become associated with specific \"starter pack\" items, its core philosophy emphasizes self-expression through a curated \"artist’s uniform\" that rejects high-fashion elitism in favor of thrifted or DIY looks.",
    "Core Apparel and Silhouettes": "A central element of the Art Hoe wardrobe is the use of high-waisted \"mom jeans\" or relaxed-fit denim trousers, often cuffed at the ankles. These are frequently paired with cropped tops, oversized sweaters, or striped long-sleeve shirts that evoke a 1990s or early 2000s \"artsy\" student look. Outerwear typically includes denim jackets, corduroy coats, or oversized cardigans in bold colors, particularly mustard yellow—a signature hue of the aesthetic. Layering is a common technique, with mesh…",
    "Footwear and Accessories": "Footwear is generally functional and durable, with Dr. Martens boots, platform sneakers, and Mary Janes being the most common choices. These are often styled with \"statement socks\" featuring embroidery, floral patterns, or replicas of famous paintings. Accessories play a significant role in defining the look; canvas tote bags are preferred over structured purses, often adorned with pins, patches, or hand-painted designs. Other notable accessories include rimless or \"Harry Potter-style\" wire…",
    "Hair and Makeup": "The approach to grooming is typically described as \"effortlessly creative.\" Makeup often incorporates unconventional colors or artistic flourishes, such as faux freckles, small painted shapes (like hearts or flowers) on the cheekbones, and bright eyeshadow in primary colors. Hair is frequently kept in natural textures or styled in \"space buns\" and short bobs, often dyed in pastel or vibrant shades to contrast with the more traditional elements of the outfit."
  },
